commit 1ece97ab9c5e4b8ffa5995b8a3d68c4ad61cb13d
ndt: start the heartbeat on an external control plane only after a drop check

A throwaway bmv2 now loads each program an external package's switches
run, with no controller and no table entries, and one heartbeat frame is
injected on every data port. The heartbeat starts only when every frame
is dropped; a program that forwards, punts, digests, clones or
multicasts it, or a check that cannot tell, leaves the heartbeat off and
ndt up and ndt status say why. Results are cached per program. The
check runs as the caller in its own directory, on a port outside the
lab's, under a name no switch-finding code matches.


